{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and your mailbox is fine. Please try these steps: 1) Fully close Outlook and reopen it. Shared mailboxes are added automatically once access applies, which can take up to an hour after access is granted. 2) If orders@ still does not appear, open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com) and check whether orders@ is listed there under Add shared folder or mailbox. 3) If it is still missing, reply to this ticket and tell us: whether you were recently given access to orders@, whether it appears in Outlook on the web, and whether you need to send email as orders@ (that needs a separate Send As permission). If you were never granted access, the orders@ mailbox owner needs to approve it first, and then our team can make the change.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for james.oconnor (user_id 8): account active, not blocked, no failed logins, mailbox 29.7% used so not a quota issue. Device BL-DT-0108 is listed as offline with last check-in 2026-10-11 01:29 UTC, no disk or warnings; may simply be powered off, not confirmed as a cause. I have no tool to verify orders@ shared mailbox permissions, so I could not confirm whether access was granted (KB-011 quick check 1). Asked user to restart Outlook, check OWA, and confirm whether access was recently granted. If access was never granted, the mailbox owner must approve and Tier 2 makes the change (KB-006 per KB-011). Send As is a separate permission. Next step: await user reply; if not granted, escalate to Tier 2. No action queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
